--- tick 2026-09-28T07:30:35+05:30 ---
STATE: ADVANCED. T-044 scope WIDENED from one site to three.
ROOT CAUSE RESTATED, and this replaces 'the window is the defect':
  AN OPERATION ASSUMES THE LOCK DIRECTORY IT RESOLVED EARLIER IS STILL THE ONE IT
  OWNS. $LOCK_DIR is a path re-resolved at every use; nothing binds a holder to
  the directory it created. Three sites, one fix.
  Site 1 = ISS-111, the acquire window (already in the brief).
  Site 2 = ISS-113 (medium, NEW): write_owner ends mv -f "$tmp"
    "$LOCK_DIR/owner" (line 176), resolving $LOCK_DIR fresh at write time. A
    slow holder B still inside write_owner when waiter A breaks and re-mkdirs
    lands its mv in A'S NEW DIRECTORY, overwriting A's owner file with B's PID.
    A's lock then NAMES THE WRONG PROCESS. The atomic temp+mv prevents torn
    reads - a real previously-fixed bug - and does nothing about the path being
    resolved twice.
  Site 3 = ISS-112 (high, NEW): release() is a bare rm -rf "$LOCK_DIR" under
    trap release EXIT, NO OWNERSHIP CHECK. After ANY break the broken-from
    holder is still alive and still trapped and on exit deletes WHOEVER HOLDS
    THE PATH THEN. A breaks B, acquires; B exits and removes A's LIVE lock; C
    acquires while A runs. EVERY BREAK CASCADES TO >=2 CONCURRENT HOLDERS AND
    THE CASCADE OUTLIVES ITS CAUSE.
WHY THIS CHANGED THE SCOPE CALL: fixing only the window removes one entrance and
  leaves the amplifier, so the failure that matters (two concurrent pnpm -r test
  = the ISS-109 OOM condition = a fake packages/db regression) SURVIVES THE FIX.
  It is also why the remedy is 'close the window', not 'widen the threshold':
  widening cuts the RATE of breaks and leaves each one just as damaging.
MECHANISM SENT TO THE BUILDER: mint a token at acquire, write it into the minimal
  owner file, hold it in a variable, and have BOTH the enrich step and release()
  verify it before acting. Makes 'is this still my directory' checkable, which it
  currently is nowhere. Fail-first regression tests required for both new sites.
  Told the builder NOT to widen further: the RAM gate's advisory nature, the 10s
  threshold, and the liveness/recycled-PID logic all stay exactly as they are.
FIGURE CORRECTED (peer, accepted): headroom is ~3x not 2.3x - a waiter re-tests
  only every POLL_SECS (5s, line 85) and the break needs age to EXCEED 10s.
  Independent timing: self_winpid 136-530ms, proc_start_ticks 2051-2732ms.
  Conclusion unchanged - a cold PowerShell start over 10s was ordinary last night.
CAUSAL LINK TO ISS-109, verified: wait_for_ram gates on MIN_FREE_GB default 2.0
  (line 86). Free physical was 1.69 GB when the peer ran the suite by hand, so
  the committed path would have logged the shortfall and waited. PEER'S OWN
  QUALIFICATION, which makes it credible: the gate is ADVISORY - after 15 retries
  it returns 0 and runs anyway. So it would have DELAYED AND ANNOUNCED, not
